{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in one of two storages, chosen when it is created:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let nexus = Nexus()                       \/\/ the default, same as Nexus(storage: .archetype)","let churning = Nexus(storage: .sparseSet) \/\/ for heavy add\/remove churn"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both storages offer the same API with the same observable behavior: generational entity identifiers, events, the structural lock and its traps, families, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"type":"text","text":", spans, snapshots, cloning and the entity state machine. Every test of the package runs against both. What differs is where the components live in memory, and with it what is cheap."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","isActive":true},{"text":", so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Nexus()"},{"type":"text","text":" uses it. Choose "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" explicitly for workloads dominated by heavy component add and remove churn (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). There is no storage protocol: the set of storages is closed, and a nexus switches on its storage once per call, so each storage compiles to concrete code."}]},{"text":"The sparse-set storage","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"The-sparse-set-storage"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keeps one dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type that maps an entity to its slot in that array, and a bitset of component types per entity. Adding or removing a component touches the data of that one type only, and no other component moves. Looking up one component is a sparse index read plus an array read."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family is the weak spot: the members of a family are stored in each component array in the order the components were added, so every extra component type costs a lookup per member, and the reads are scattered once the arrays were shuffled by churn."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"The archetype storage","anchor":"The-archetype-storage"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" follows the design of "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","type":"reference"},{"text":": entities with exactly the same component types live in one table, with a column (an array) per component type. An index maps every entity to its table and row. Tables are created when a component set appears first, and adding or removing one component type moves the entity’s row to another table along a cached edge of the table graph.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating a family visits the tables that match it, and walks their columns linearly: no lookup per member and a sequential read per component. The list of matching tables is cached per family, which the nexus lists when the family is created and extends when a new table appears. A table that became empty stays alive, along with its columns and its entry in the cached lists, where an iteration skips it. Cleaning the nexus with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drops all tables."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In flecs this is the default, and sparse components are the opt-in trait ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sparse"},{"type":"text","text":"): “Sparse components are stored outside of tables, which means they do not have to be moved”, trading query speed for component add and remove speed (see "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). Fireblade 1.x was the reverse, a sparse set per component type; the two storages make that a choice per nexus instead of per component.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What the numbers say","anchor":"What-the-numbers-say"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Measured with 10 000 entities, release build, Apple silicon, wall clock p50 per pass ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"make benchmark"},{"type":"text","text":", see "},{"code":"Benchmarks\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","alignments":["left","right","right"],"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Case"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sparse set"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Archetype"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2.5 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.3 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, C, D)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"31 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"7.7 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, writing: B)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"17 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.4 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, writing: C)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"23 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"6.1 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 10% of the entities match"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"3.6 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.3 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 100 000 entities with shuffled storage order"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"227 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"27 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 1 024 different component sets"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter pack, 5 reads and 2 writes"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 200 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 800 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":" over a family, 2 components"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Random "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity.get"},{"type":"text","text":" of one component, 10 000 lookups"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"334 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"345 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a component to each entity and remove it again, 10 000 entities"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 180 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4 900 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create and destroy 1 000 entities with 7 components"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"1 730 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 510 μs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fireblade 1.x needed 480 μs for the plain iteration of one component and 1 220 μs for two ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IterOnlyOneComponent"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IterOnlyTwoComponents"},{"type":"text","text":"). Both storages iterate without any allocation."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterating with ","type":"text"},{"code":"forEach(reading:writing:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is 1.6 to 8 times faster on the archetype storage: about 4 times in the plain case, 8 times when the sparse-set arrays are shuffled against each other, and least when the entities are spread over many small tables."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changing the component set of an entity costs about twice as much on the archetype storage: the whole row moves. An entity that changes its component set less than once in a few frames is far ahead on iteration; a world that toggles a component on most entities every frame is better off with the sparse set."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":" iteration and random access cost the same on both: they look every component up per entity."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entity creation and destruction are a bit slower on the archetype storage, because the row of every component moves with the entity."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Which storage to pick","anchor":"Which-storage-to-pick"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default is the archetype storage: it iterates faster (see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"), and iteration is what most worlds spend their time on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The trade-off: the archetype storage buys iteration speed with the cost of moving a row whenever the component set of an entity changes. Prefer ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" when the workload is dominated by heavy add and remove churn, for example toggling a component on most entities every frame. This matches flecs, where sparse components are the opt-in trait for components that are added and removed often.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Differences you can observe","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Differences-you-can-observe"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration order."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The sparse-set storage visits the members of a family in the order of the family’s member list, the archetype storage table by table and row by row, and rows move when entities change tables. Neither order is a contract; use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or your own key if you need one.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Single-type spans."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" view one contiguous array. On the archetype storage a type is stored in one column per table, so if entities with different component sets have the type, the span views a temporary copy made table by table (and the writing variant stores it back when the closure returns, also when it throws). That costs one allocation and a copy per call, and nothing can observe the difference while the closure runs, because the type is locked.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Family spans."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" passes one batch per matching table on the archetype storage, however the nexus was used before; the sparse-set storage passes shorter batches after churn. Both visit every member exactly once, and the closure must be correct for any batch size.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","isActive":true},{"text":" for the spans.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"anchor":"Essentials"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"title":"Choosing a storage","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and know what changes."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage"]}],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Nexus"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","title":"Nexus","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Nexus"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventMask":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The kinds of events a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" subscribes to."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventMask"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventMask"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventmask","title":"NexusEventMask","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReadingAndWritingComponents":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/readingandwritingcomponents","title":"Reading and writing components","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read a copy, replace a component or change it in place."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","title":"Which storage to pick","type":"topic","kind":"section","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage#Which-storage-to-pick","abstract":[]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/clear()":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/clear()","title":"clear()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clears all data from the Nexus."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clear","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(writing:_:)":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","title":"componentSpan(writing:_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gives "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" write access to all components of a type as one contiguous "},{"code":"MutableSpan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"componentSpan","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"genericParameter"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"writing"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type, ("},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s11MutableSpanV","text":"MutableSpan","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Result"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(writing:_:)"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Family/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"each C"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Component"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"title":"forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterates the members of this family in batches, giving "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"text":" the components of a batch as contiguous spans.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"forEachComponentSpan"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"R1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W1"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"reading"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"R1"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"writing"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W1"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type, ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Span","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"R1"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MutableSpan","preciseIdentifier":"s:s11MutableSpanV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W1"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Void","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/family\/foreachcomponentspan(reading:writing:_:)"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS","title":"FirebladeECS","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A lightweight, fast and easy to use Entity-Component System in Swift."}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs"},"https://www.flecs.dev/flecs/md_docs_2Queries.html":{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","url":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","type":"link","title":"flecs","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"flecs"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(reading:_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(reading:_:)","title":"componentSpan(reading:_:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" read access to all components of a type as one contiguous "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Span"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"componentSpan"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Result"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"reading"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"text":".Type, (","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV","text":"Span","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Result","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rethrows","kind":"keyword"}